;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; THREE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the British Crown, via Companies House
;;   * the issuer itself, at the website blueprint.edn records for it
;;
;; THE ISRAELI HOME REGISTER IS NOT AMONG THEM -- BUT ITS NUMBER IS STILL
;; CORROBORATED, AND THAT IS THE DIFFERENCE FROM THE SIBLINGS IN THIS FAMILY.
;;
;; GLEIF names RA000406 -- the Israeli Corporations Authority (Department of
;; Justice) -- as BOTH the register of record and the validation authority for
;; this entity (rows gleif-registered-at-ra and gleif-validated-at-ra), and gives
;; the Israeli company number as 520018078. That register could not be cited
;; directly: every route to it is recorded by name under :catalog/unreachable
;; below, and none of them was worked around.
;;
;; What makes this catalog different from, say, the Reliance sibling -- where the
;; home registration number rested on GLEIF's word ALONE -- is that here a SECOND
;; state prints it. Companies House, asked about the UK subsidiary, publishes its
;; person with significant control and records, in the UK register's own words:
;;
;;     Place registered      Israeli Companies Register
;;     Registration number   52-001807
;;     Governing law         Israeli Law
;;     Incorporated in       Israel
;;
;; 52-001807 is 520018078 without its trailing check digit, hyphenated in the UK
;; style. So the most load-bearing identifier in this catalog is attested by two
;; authorities that did not consult each other: GLEIF and the British Crown.
;; It is NOT a byte-for-byte match, and rows uk-psc-registration-number and
;; gleif-registered-as deliberately carry both forms so the difference is visible
;; rather than smoothed over.
;;
;; THE CHAIN THAT MAKES THAT POSSIBLE. GLEIF records exactly one direct child of
;; this LEI: BANK LEUMI (U.K.) P.L.C., LEI 549300DBFNYYFVRXVB58, UK company
;; 00640370 (rows gleif-child-*). Companies House prints that same name and that
;; same number in its own record (uk-ch-name, uk-ch-number). Following that child
;; to its PSC page is what produces the Israeli number above.
;;
;; THREE PLACES WHERE THE TWO AUTHORITIES DO NOT AGREE. These are recorded, not
;; reconciled, because the disagreement is itself the finding:
;;
;;   THE NAME. The UK register calls the controller "Bank Leumi Le Israel B.M".
;;   GLEIF's CURRENT legal name is "BANK LEUMI LE-ISRAEL LTD."; it carries
;;   "BANK LEUMI LE-ISRAEL B.M." only as a PREVIOUS legal name, with a completed
;;   CHANGE_LEGAL_NAME event effective 2022-07-19. The UK entry, notified in 2016,
;;   still carries the pre-2022 name. Rows uk-psc-parent-name,
;;   gleif-previous-name-bm and gleif-name-change-event hold all three facts.
;;
;;   THE ADDRESS. The UK register gives 34 Yehuda Halevi Street, Tel Aviv. GLEIF
;;   gives 3 ABA HILLEL SILVER ST, LOD, after a CHANGE_LEGAL_ADDRESS event
;;   effective 2024-04-19. The UK correspondence address is therefore NOT a second
;;   witness to the current address -- it is a witness to the old one.
;;
;;   THE CHILD'S STATUS. GLEIF returns BANK LEUMI (U.K.) P.L.C. as an ACTIVE
;;   entity in its direct-children collection. Companies House says the company
;;   status is Liquidation. Row uk-ch-status-liquidation records what the UK
;;   register says; no row asserts the child is trading.
;;
;; THE TASE LISTING IS CITED SECOND-HAND. Row uk-psc-legal-form is the UK register
;; describing the controller as "A Banking Corporation With Shares Listed On The
;; Tel Aviv Stock Exchange". That is the ONLY citation here for the exchange
;; listing: TASE's own systems could not be cited (see :catalog/unreachable), so
;; no row in this catalog is the exchange speaking for itself.
;;
;; THE ISSUER NAMES ITSELF, IN HEBREW ONLY. The bank's privacy policy opens with
;; the Hebrew legal name (row leumi-legal-name-he). GLEIF holds the English form
;; and an EMPTY transliteratedOtherNames list, so the join from the Hebrew name to
;; the GLEIF record runs through transliteration, not through a shared string. The
;; issuer does not publish its company number on the pages reached here.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before the
;; claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or a specific
;;               related legal entity. Point the URL at a different company and
;;               the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT (status
;;               ACTIVE, country IL, governing law Israeli Law, SIC 64191). Such a
;;               row can survive a swap to a similar company. It is recorded
;;               because it is true and checkable, not because it identifies.
;;
;; THE TAXONOMY IS MEASURED, NOT ASSERTED. Every row above was classified by
;; repointing the GLEIF URL at BANK HAPOALIM (LEI B6ARUI4946ST4S7WOU88) -- a real
;; Israeli bank of comparable size, same country, same ACTIVE status -- and seeing
;; which rows survived. THREE rows drafted as :identity survived that swap and
;; were demoted to :attribute before this file landed:
;;
;;   gleif-managing-lou        both banks are managed by the same LOU
;;   gleif-registered-at-ra    RA000406 is the register for every Israeli company
;;   gleif-validated-at-ra     same
;;
;; No row that claims :identity survives being pointed at another company.
;;
;; Counting rows is not counting evidence. Nine of the :identity rows and nineteen
;; of the :attribute rows come from a SINGLE GLEIF document -- 28 of the 56 rows
;; here are one authority speaking once, not 28 witnesses.

